<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fiesole</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fiesole is a hill town overlooking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> in Tuscany, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. Founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruscans">Etruscans</a> and later a Roman town, it was older than Florence and long its rival, until the Florentines conquered and destroyed it in 1125. It preserves a Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> and Etruscan walls, and its villas and views made it a favourite retreat of wealthy Florentines.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fiesole.jpg" alt="Fiesole" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hagai Agmon-Snir حچاي اچمون-سنير חגי אגמון-שניר · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FiesoleDec102023_15.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
